  "notes": "Integrated stereo amplifier, 80 W RMS into 8 ohms. Everything from the CXA61/81 manual (Rear panel connections, Front panel controls, Remote control, Specifications); the rear panel drawing gives D1 and D2 as Toslink optical and D3 as S/P DIF coaxial. Bluetooth (aptX HD) is an input without a socket, so it is only a SOURCE position here. Controls: the source buttons (on the CXA81 the A1 button toggles between the unbalanced RCA and the balanced XLR A1 input), Speaker A/B (A, B or A and B), Mute (remote control), Volume ('affects the level of all outputs', so the pre-out and sub out follow it), and the USB Ground/Lift switch, which only helps against hum. From the manual: plugging in headphones mutes the loudspeaker, pre-out and sub outputs; the sub out is low-pass filtered (about 2.3 kHz). Left out: the AC power inlet, RS232C, Control Bus, IR in and the 12 V trigger in/out, the Bluetooth antenna, and the standby button. Volume at MIN is treated as silent; start positions (A1, speakers A, volume low) are app defaults. Socket genders are not stated; female assumed.",
